    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR01, 0U, "DR-01-RS-0001", "Disk Recovery Index", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_DR01_DISK_RECOVERY_INDEX, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T001, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE RECOVERY ENVIRONMENT\nDISK 144 - RECOVERY INDEX\n\nMedium status: readable with losses.\nSource: closure-period working copy, Site identifier partially unrecoverable.\nRecovered classes: correspondence, registers, plans, equipment records, access records and selected spatial references.\n\nThe source medium is not a complete copy of the Departmental archive. File headers may survive where body text does not. Room and object positions are reconstructed only where surviving records provide sufficient agreement.\n\nOperators are reminded that absence from this medium is evidence of absence from this medium only.\n\nWHAT VERSION OF THE TRUTH ARE YOU WILLING TO ACCEPT?", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR01, 3U, "DR-01-RS-0035", "Terminal Access & Command Reference", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE RECOVERY ENVIRONMENT\nTERMINAL QUICK REFERENCE\n\nINITIATE      Mount the recovered archive and prepare the working index.\nLIST          Display collections presently available to the operator.\nRESTORE code  Recover the named collection into the current working set.\nOPEN record   Display the recovered text associated with a record identifier.\nEXIT          Leave the terminal and return to the Site view.\n\nCommands do not alter the source medium. Where only catalogue metadata survives, the terminal will identify the record but will not manufacture missing text.\n\nOperator note: a failed OPEN request is not proof that the original document never existed.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR01, 4U, "DR-01-RS-0049", "Collection Restoration", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE RECOVERY ENVIRONMENT\nCOLLECTION RESTORATION NOTE\n\nThe working environment has less storage than the total amount of recoverable material identified on Disk 144. Collections are therefore restored selectively.\n\nOnce a collection has been admitted to the working set, its recovered records and any corroborated Site references remain available for the duration of that recovery session. Restoration cannot be rolled back to reclaim space.\n\nThe system may reconstruct rooms, objects or labels from surviving administrative references. Such reconstructions indicate that the item was recorded, not that every recorded detail is correct.\n\nWhere records disagree, retain the disagreement.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR01, 6U, "DR-01-RS-0072", "Listing & Opening Records", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE RECOVERY ENVIRONMENT\nCATALOGUE AND RECORD HANDLING\n\nThe catalogue and the documents are separate survivals.\n\nA catalogue entry may retain a title, reference and filing location after the document body has been lost. Conversely, a recovered text fragment may survive without all of its original catalogue fields. The recovery terminal preserves both conditions rather than filling gaps by assumption.\n\nUse LIST to locate a collection and OPEN with the full record reference to inspect available text.\n\nDo not treat a tidy index as a tidy history.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR02, 1U, "DR-02-RS-0016", "Terminal Access & Command Reference", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nINFORMATION SYSTEMS CIRCULAR\nTERMINAL ACCESS & COMMAND REFERENCE\n\nArchive recovery terminals are intended for supervised examination of damaged departmental media. The source device is mounted read-only.\n\nNormal sequence:\n1. INITIATE the recovery environment.\n2. LIST available holdings.\n3. RESTORE only the collections required for the current examination.\n4. OPEN individual record references as required.\n5. EXIT before removing power or changing media.\n\nRepeated commands are harmless. Repeated assumptions are not.\n\nFaults affecting the terminal itself are to be logged separately from faults found in the recovered archive.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR02, 2U, "DR-02-RS-0029", "Archive Command Syntax", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTERMINAL OPERATIONS GUIDE\nARCHIVE COMMAND SYNTAX\n\nCommands are entered as plain text and are not case-sensitive.\n\nINITIATE\nStarts archive services and verifies the mounted recovery medium.\n\nLIST\nPrints the currently visible collection codes and recovery status.\n\nRESTORE XX-00\nCopies recoverable material for the named collection into the working area.\n\nOPEN XX-00-RS-0000\nDisplays the selected recovered record.\n\nEXIT\nCloses the terminal session without writing to the source medium.\n\nDo not abbreviate record identifiers. A valid-looking reference can still point to a record whose body was not recovered.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR02, 3U, "DR-02-RS-0037", "Error & Recovery Messages", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTERMINAL OPERATIONS GUIDE\nERROR & RECOVERY MESSAGES\n\nNO SUCH COLLECTION\nThe catalogue does not contain the requested collection code.\n\nCOLLECTION NOT AVAILABLE\nThe holding exists but its current dependencies have not been recovered.\n\nRECORD BODY UNRECOVERABLE\nCatalogue metadata survives; readable content does not.\n\nRECOVERY CAPACITY EXCEEDED\nThe working set cannot accept further restored material.\n\nCHECKSUM DISAGREEMENT\nTwo recovered copies differ. Neither copy is to be silently preferred.\n\nSESSION NOT INITIALISED\nRun INITIATE before archive commands.\n\nOperators are to record recurring checksum faults, not cure them with imagination.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR02, 4U, "DR-02-RS-0045", "Terminal Session Safeguards", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTERMINAL OPERATIONS GUIDE\nTERMINAL SESSION SAFEGUARDS\n\nThe recovery terminal must never write to original media.\n\nSession history is temporary and is cleared when the recovery environment is closed. Recovered documents remain unchanged by viewing. Notes made by the examiner are held in the working session only unless separately exported.\n\nIf a record appears inconsistent with a reconstructed room or object, inspect the physical reference and retain both observations.\n\nDo not:\n- rename damaged records for convenience;\n- infer missing signatures;\n- merge contradictory versions;\n- treat an access failure as evidence of wrongdoing.\n\nPreservation includes preserving uncertainty.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR03, 1U, "DR-03-RS-0025", "Reconstruction & Collection Recovery Procedures", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE RECOVERY UNIT\nRECONSTRUCTION & COLLECTION RECOVERY PROCEDURES\n\nSite reconstruction is derived from surviving room schedules, asset registers, access plans, desk allocations and maintenance records.\n\nA room is admitted to the working model only when the recovery system has enough independent references to place it with reasonable confidence. Movable items require a recorded location or a surviving physical association. Decorative detail is omitted unless specifically evidenced.\n\nRecovered collections may add new references and therefore improve the Site model.\n\nThe resulting Site is an evidential aid. It is not a photograph, a memory, or permission to assume what the records do not say.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR03, 2U, "DR-03-RS-0033", "Reconstruction Quota Notes", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE RECOVERY UNIT\nWORKING-CAPACITY NOTE\n\nDisk 144 contains more recoverable material than can be expanded into one working recovery.\n\nPriority is therefore determined by the examiner. Essential administrative chains should be restored before peripheral holdings. When the working capacity is exhausted, the session is to end with a record of what was recovered and what remains outside the current working set.\n\nCapacity limits are technical, not evidential. Material omitted because there was no room for it has not thereby become irrelevant.\n\nA second recovery may produce a different but equally valid view of the same source medium.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR03, 3U, "DR-03-RS-0046", "Physical Item Reconstruction Rules", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE RECOVERY UNIT\nPHYSICAL-REFERENCE RECONSTRUCTION RULES\n\nPhysical items may be represented in the Site model where one or more surviving records identify both the object and its location.\n\nExamples include labelled folders, equipment panels, access cards, desk notes, transfer boxes and cabinet markers.\n\nA reconstructed item means:\n- the archive says an item of that description was there;\n- the location is sufficiently supported to be useful;\n- the object may be examined alongside the documentary record.\n\nIt does not mean:\n- the item is complete;\n- every label is legible;\n- its recorded purpose was its actual use.\n\nWhere an object contradicts a document, keep looking.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR03, 4U, "DR-03-RS-0054", "Evidence & Notebook Behaviour", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE RECOVERY UNIT\nEXAMINER'S NOTEBOOK GUIDANCE\n\nThe recovery environment may copy confirmed observations into the examiner's Notebook. Entries should be factual and should identify what has actually been established.\n\nGood: \"The transfer box was on the Records Trolley.\"\nPoor: \"Someone hid the transfer box.\"\n\nGood: \"No visitor entry was recorded for the restricted area.\"\nPoor: \"No visitor entered the restricted area.\"\n\nThe Notebook is intended to prevent the examiner's memory from becoming more confident than the archive.\n\nConclusions should arise from several records, physical references and timings. Suspicion is useful. Certainty is expensive.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR04, 2U, "DR-04-RS-0037", "Outstanding Workstream Summary", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nSITE CLOSURE PROJECT\nOUTSTANDING WORKSTREAM SUMMARY\n\nAt close of business Thursday, two operational workstreams remained capable of delaying handover.\n\nRECORDS\nCabinet holdings and transfer staging require final reconciliation in the Records Office.\n\nTECHNOLOGY\nThe Main Office terminal route must be restored before digital holdings verification can be completed.\n\nThe workstreams may proceed independently, but both feed the same final handover decision. Neither is to be marked complete on the strength of verbal assurance.\n\nFacilities and Security are to support access as required.\n\nDistribution: Martin Webb, Project Manager, Priya Patel, Senior Archivist, Claire Hughes, IT Manager, Rachel Morgan, Security Manager.", true, true },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR04, 5U, "DR-04-RS-0063", "Physical Archive Reconciliation Workstream", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T010, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nSITE CLOSURE PROJECT\nPHYSICAL ARCHIVE RECONCILIATION WORKSTREAM\n\nOwner: Priya Patel, Senior Archivist\nStatus at Friday 09:00: OPEN\n\nFinal cabinet-to-catalogue reconciliation is incomplete. Several holdings have been withdrawn for transfer, one trolley remains awaiting refiling, and the closure file contains unresolved location exceptions.\n\nRecords Office access is required for completion. The trolley, withdrawal markers and transfer staging material are to remain undisturbed until the Priya Patel, Senior Archivist has signed the exception register.\n\nHandover may not be certified while the physical holdings total differs from the signed catalogue total.\n\nProject Manager note: this is a records problem until somebody proves otherwise.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR04, 7U, "DR-04-RS-0087", "Terminal Network Remediation Workstream", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T011, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nSITE CLOSURE PROJECT\nTERMINAL NETWORK REMEDIATION WORKSTREAM\n\nOwner: IT Support\nStatus at Friday 09:00: OPEN\n\nThe Main Office archive terminal is locally serviceable but cannot complete digital verification against the server holdings. Initial tests place the fault beyond the terminal desk.\n\nIT Support is to trace the affected circuit through the local patching and onward to the Server Room route. Archive verification media has already been prepared and is not to be reused for any other purpose.\n\nHandover may not be certified until the route is restored or a formally accepted workaround is recorded.\n\nDo not replace working terminal equipment merely because it is easier to reach.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR04, 10U, "DR-04-RS-0111", "Handover Readiness Checklist", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nSITE CLOSURE PROJECT\nHANDOVER READINESS CHECKLIST\n\n[OK] Staff posting notices issued.\n[OK] Furniture and general assets marked for transfer or disposal.\n[OK] Visitor arrangements reduced to closure staffing.\n[OK] Routine utilities decommissioning scheduled.\n[  ] Physical archive reconciliation complete.\n[  ] Digital holdings verification complete.\n[  ] Final security review complete.\n[  ] Director's handover certificate signed.\n\nTwo incomplete lines have been carried forward from Thursday.\n\nProject Manager annotation:\n\"Friday is still achievable provided nobody discovers a third workstream.\"", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR04, 12U, "DR-04-RS-0137", "Final Friday Milestone Plan", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nSITE CLOSURE PROJECT\nFINAL FRIDAY MILESTONE PLAN\n\n08:30  Closure team attendance confirmed.\n09:00  Records reconciliation resumes.\n09:00  Terminal fault investigation resumes.\n11:30  Preliminary exception review.\n13:00  Archive transfer staging check.\n14:00  Digital verification window, subject to network availability.\n15:30  Security and facilities final walk-round.\n16:00  Director handover review.\n16:30  Site closure target.\n\nContingency:\nAny incident affecting restricted areas, archive custody or life safety suspends the 16:30 handover review.\n\nHandwritten note:\n\"Tea has not been given a milestone because apparently we are still a serious Department.\"", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR04, 15U, "DR-04-RS-0174", "Building Handover Dependencies", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nSITE CLOSURE PROJECT\nBUILDING HANDOVER DEPENDENCIES\n\nFinal handover requires all of the following:\n\nA. Physical holdings accounted for or recorded as authorised transfer exceptions.\nB. Digital holdings verification completed against prepared media.\nC. Restricted-area access and key custody reconciled.\nD. Essential services left in their agreed closure state.\nE. Outstanding incidents reviewed by Operational Security.\nF. Director's authority to release the building.\n\nAn incomplete dependency is not to be converted into \"not applicable\" solely to preserve the target date.\n\nThe Site will close late before it closes incorrectly.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR07, 3U, "DR-07-RS-0038", "Archive Reconciliation Exception Report", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T013, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nRECORDS OFFICE\nARCHIVE RECONCILIATION EXCEPTION REPORT\n\nException: one registered holding is not present in its assigned secure cabinet.\n\nCatalogue location: Cabinet 05.\nLast recorded action: withdrawn for internal handling.\nCurrent status: unresolved at time of report.\n\nA Records Trolley remains in use for material awaiting refiling. Staff are to check trolley holdings, dividers and temporary slips before escalating the item as missing.\n\nNo destruction authority is recorded against the reference.\n\nPriya Patel, Senior Archivist:\n\"Please stop using the word 'lost' until we have looked in the places we put things.\"", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR07, 6U, "DR-07-RS-0075", "Unlocated Holdings Schedule", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T014, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nRECORDS OFFICE\nUNLOCATED HOLDINGS SCHEDULE\n\nThe following location exception remains open:\n\nRegistered cabinet: 05\nExpected marker: external withdrawal/location card\nPhysical holding: not present at registered cabinet position\nSearch priority: trolley, active work folders, transfer staging\n\nA withdrawal marker is part of the custody trail and is not to be removed when the file itself is moved.\n\nIf the marker and the holding can be matched, amend the reconciliation sheet and return both to the Senior Archivist for sign-off.\n\nUnlocated does not mean unaccounted for. Not yet.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR07, 10U, "DR-07-RS-0112", "Trolley Holding Reconciliation", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nRECORDS OFFICE\nTROLLEY HOLDING RECONCILIATION\n\nThe Records Trolley was checked against the temporary refiling divider at 11:20.\n\nOne holding listed as absent from Cabinet 05 is present on the trolley behind the \"TO REFILE\" divider. A misfile slip is attached. The catalogue has not yet been amended.\n\nAction:\n- leave the record on the trolley;\n- retain the slip;\n- match it to the cabinet withdrawal marker;\n- obtain Senior Archivist initials before refiling.\n\nThis resolves location, not custody. The transfer batch remains a separate exercise.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR07, 13U, "DR-07-RS-0144", "Cabinet Location Audit", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nRECORDS OFFICE\nCABINET LOCATION AUDIT\n\nCabinets 01-04: no material exception noted.\nCabinet 05: one withdrawal marker present; corresponding holding not in shelf position.\nCabinet 06: transfer withdrawals in progress; see transfer register.\nOpen shelving: routine working material only.\nTrolley: awaiting full reconciliation.\n\nThe audit records where material was expected at the time of inspection. It is not a historical movement log.\n\nWhere a cabinet position is empty and a marker is present, follow the marker before raising an incident report.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR07, 17U, "DR-07-RS-0186", "Refiling Exception Notes", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nRECORDS OFFICE\nREFILING EXCEPTION NOTES\n\nThree causes of temporary location mismatch were recorded during closure work:\n\n1. material removed for transfer-box preparation;\n2. material held on the trolley pending index amendment;\n3. material returned to the wrong divider after consultation.\n\nNone of the three automatically constitutes a custody failure.\n\nAll closure-period refiling is to use a written slip, even for movements within the Records Office. The rule has been reissued because \"I'll remember where I put it\" has again failed audit.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR07, 20U, "DR-07-RS-0223", "Archive Reconciliation Sign-off", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nRECORDS OFFICE\nARCHIVE RECONCILIATION SIGN-OFF\n\nPhysical count: substantially complete.\nOpen exceptions: transfer batch and one trolley-held record.\nUnexplained losses: NONE CONFIRMED.\nDestruction discrepancies: NONE RECORDED.\n\nFinal sign-off withheld pending:\n- transfer manifest comparison;\n- custody-sheet completion;\n- return or formal relocation of trolley-held material.\n\nPrepared by: Daniel Price, Records Officer\nFor review by: Priya Patel, Senior Archivist\n\nMargin note:\n\"Do not sign the bottom box until the top boxes mean what they say.\"", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR23, 2U, "DR-23-RS-0034", "1962 Initial Filing Discrepancy", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nHISTORICAL EXCEPTIONS FILE\n12 OCTOBER 1962 - INITIAL FILING DISCREPANCY\n\nDuring the morning Top Secret holdings check, file TS/4/118 was not found in its registered box.\n\nThe index card showed no authorised withdrawal. Duty staff searched the immediate cabinet run twice without result. The discrepancy was reported to the Site Security Officer at 10:42.\n\nPending investigation, no conclusion was reached as to loss, removal or misfiling.\n\nThe original report contains the handwritten addition:\n\"Please establish location before establishing culprit.\"", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR23, 4U, "DR-23-RS-0055", "1962 Site Lockdown Direction", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nHISTORICAL EXCEPTIONS FILE\n12 OCTOBER 1962 - SITE LOCKDOWN DIRECTION\n\nFollowing the unresolved absence of TS/4/118, outward movement of classified records is suspended.\n\nAll exits are to be controlled. Staff leaving the Site are to be identified and recorded. Archive boxes in the affected sequence are not to be rearranged.\n\nThis direction is precautionary and does not imply deliberate removal.\n\nReview interval: every six hours.\nMaximum initial duration: 72 hours without Director approval.\n\nSecurity Officer annotation:\n\"The building is closed. The filing cabinets remain, regrettably, at liberty.\"", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR23, 7U, "DR-23-RS-0092", "1962 Misfile Recovery Record", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nHISTORICAL EXCEPTIONS FILE\n15 OCTOBER 1962 - MISFILE RECOVERY RECORD\n\nFile TS/4/118 was recovered at 07:35 from box TS/4/181.\n\nThe outer folders are visually similar and had been returned during a high-volume consultation period. No evidence of removal from the secure archive was found. The file contents and page count were complete.\n\nThe Site lockdown was lifted at 08:10.\n\nCause recorded: transposition during refiling.\n\nNo disciplinary action recommended beyond procedural review and one extremely pointed reminder concerning box numbers.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR23, 9U, "DR-23-RS-0108", "1962 Procedural Review", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nHISTORICAL EXCEPTIONS FILE\n1962 PROCEDURAL REVIEW\n\nFinding:\nThe incident arose from a filing transposition, compounded by an index that recorded expected location but not the most recent handling step.\n\nActions approved:\n- temporary withdrawal slips for all classified consultations;\n- independent check of returned holdings;\n- clearer box-number typography;\n- escalation language to distinguish \"not located\" from \"lost\".\n\nReview conclusion:\nA serious discrepancy deserves a serious response. It does not deserve a preferred explanation before the search is complete.\n\nThis case is retained for training because certainty arrived three days later than suspicion.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR29, 2U, "DR-29-RS-0009", "Final Transfer Batch Custody Register", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T015, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE TRANSFER TEAM\nFINAL TRANSFER BATCH CUSTODY REGISTER\n\nBatch: FINAL-6\nStatus: staged in Records Office\n\nThe listed holdings have been deliberately withdrawn from normal cabinet storage for transfer preparation. Each withdrawal must be represented by a cabinet marker and must remain traceable to a labelled transfer box.\n\nCustody passes from Records Officer to Senior Archivist only when the manifest, seal number and holding count agree.\n\nAn empty cabinet position within this batch is therefore expected.\n\nDo not refile transfer material merely to make the cabinet look complete.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR29, 5U, "DR-29-RS-0046", "Transfer Box Manifest", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T016, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE TRANSFER TEAM\nTRANSFER BOX MANIFEST\n\nBox: FINAL-6-B\nPrepared: Friday\n\nContents checked against transfer list.\nIndividual holding references: see attached sheet.\nTemporary withdrawal markers: to remain in source cabinets until receipt is confirmed.\nSeal: to be applied after Senior Archivist verification.\nDestination: central archive intake.\n\nThe box is staged on the Records Trolley pending final custody signature.\n\nA sealed box without a signed manifest is not a completed transfer. It is merely a box that has become harder to inspect.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR29, 8U, "DR-29-RS-0083", "Archive Transfer Staging Plan", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE TRANSFER TEAM\nARCHIVE TRANSFER STAGING PLAN\n\nClosure-period transfer material is to be assembled on the Records Trolley by batch.\n\nSequence:\n1. withdraw holding and place marker in cabinet;\n2. compare reference with transfer list;\n3. place holding in labelled box;\n4. prepare manifest;\n5. obtain Senior Archivist verification;\n6. seal box;\n7. record handover.\n\nThe trolley is a controlled staging point, not an alternative filing system.\n\nNormal refiling and transfer staging must not share the same divider.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR29, 11U, "DR-29-RS-0118", "Custody Seal Register", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE TRANSFER TEAM\nCUSTODY SEAL REGISTER\n\nUnused seals remain with the Daniel Price, Records Officer.\nApplied seals are entered against box number, date, time and witness.\n\nFINAL-6-B: seal reserved, NOT YET APPLIED.\nReason: verification outstanding.\n\nAny seal removed after application is to be retained and attached to the exception sheet.\n\nThere is no requirement to seal an incomplete box for the convenience of the closure timetable.\n\nUnsigned correction in margin:\n\"Nor does writing 'FINAL' on something make it final.\"", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR29, 14U, "DR-29-RS-0153", "Transfer Batch Exception Note", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE TRANSFER TEAM\nTRANSFER BATCH EXCEPTION NOTE\n\nBatch FINAL-6 cannot be released.\n\nReason:\nOne physical reconciliation exception remains open and the corresponding digital verification has not been completed. The transfer box is otherwise prepared.\n\nRequired before release:\n- confirm the location and custody status of the outstanding holding;\n- complete digital holdings comparison;\n- Senior Archivist signature.\n\nThe exception is administrative. No loss or compromise is asserted by this note.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR29, 17U, "DR-29-RS-0188", "Digital Verification Dependency", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE TRANSFER TEAM\nDIGITAL VERIFICATION DEPENDENCY\n\nPhysical transfer and digital verification are paired closure controls.\n\nThe paper manifest confirms what is intended to leave the Site. The verification media confirms that the corresponding digital holdings were prepared and checked before systems are withdrawn.\n\nA completed physical box does not waive the digital check.\nA completed checksum does not account for a physical file.\n\nBoth records are required before the Senior Archivist may release the final batch.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR31, 2U, "DR-31-RS-0031", "Final Transfer Exception Register", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T017, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE TRANSFER AUTHORITY\nFINAL TRANSFER EXCEPTION REGISTER\n\nOpen at 12:00 Friday:\n\nEX-1  Cabinet 05 holding on trolley pending refiling confirmation.\nEX-2  Final transfer box awaiting custody verification.\nEX-3  Digital holdings check blocked by network fault.\n\nOwner for closure: Priya Patel, Senior Archivist.\n\nNo exception is marked as suspected interference. All remain operationally unresolved.\n\nThe register is to be reviewed with the Project Manager before handover, or immediately following any incident that interrupts the closure programme.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR31, 5U, "DR-31-RS-0068", "Senior Archivist Verification Assignment", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T018, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE TRANSFER AUTHORITY\nSENIOR ARCHIVIST VERIFICATION ASSIGNMENT\n\nFor the final closure period, the Senior Archivist is personally assigned to verify:\n\n- physical transfer exceptions;\n- custody signatures;\n- final transfer-box contents;\n- digital holdings comparison;\n- any variance between cabinet, trolley and manifest.\n\nRestricted-area access may be requested where necessary to complete digital verification or inspect systems supporting the archive.\n\nThis assignment is a control measure, not a change of post.\n\nThe Senior Archivist is not to delegate final signature to staff whose work is being verified.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR31, 7U, "DR-31-RS-0092", "Custody Exception Sign-off", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE TRANSFER AUTHORITY\nCUSTODY EXCEPTION SIGN-OFF\n\nException sign-off requires three questions to be answered:\n\nWhere is the holding?\nWho has custody?\nWhy does that differ from the normal catalogue location?\n\nIf all three answers are documented and authorised, the location variance may be closed without treating it as a loss.\n\nIf any answer depends on recollection alone, retain the exception.\n\nFinal closure has produced an unusual quantity of temporary movement. The purpose of the register is to make temporary movement visible, not suspicious by default.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR31, 10U, "DR-31-RS-0129", "Unverified Holdings List", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE TRANSFER AUTHORITY\nUNVERIFIED HOLDINGS LIST\n\nThe following categories remain outside final verification:\n\n- material in the last transfer box;\n- records represented by temporary withdrawal markers;\n- one trolley-held refiling exception;\n- digital holdings awaiting server comparison.\n\nThis list is deliberately broader than the incident list.\n\nUnverified means the closure check is incomplete. It does not mean the underlying holding is damaged, missing or compromised.\n\nNext review: after network service is restored or at 15:00, whichever occurs first.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR31, 12U, "DR-31-RS-0142", "Handover Authority Note", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE TRANSFER AUTHORITY\nHANDOVER AUTHORITY NOTE\n\nThe Director may accept the building only after receiving the Senior Archivist's completed transfer release and the Project Manager's closure certificate.\n\nWhere an incident occurs before signature, existing release authority lapses until Security has completed an initial review.\n\nNo officer is authorised to back-date a handover certificate to the planned closure time.\n\nThe planned time is a target, not a historical fact.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR31, 15U, "DR-31-RS-0168", "Transfer Release Checklist", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nARCHIVE TRANSFER AUTHORITY\nTRANSFER RELEASE CHECKLIST\n\n[  ] Physical exceptions reconciled\n[  ] Transfer manifest agreed\n[  ] Custody sheet signed\n[  ] Box seal applied and recorded\n[  ] Digital verification complete\n[  ] Security exceptions cleared\n[  ] Senior Archivist release signed\n\nStatus at time of filing: INCOMPLETE\n\nInstruction:\nLeave unchecked boxes unchecked. The receiving archive would rather inherit an honest delay than an immaculate fiction.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR47, 2U, "DR-47-RS-0006", "Final Closure Exception Summary", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T026, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nSITE CLOSURE PROJECT\nFINAL CLOSURE EXCEPTION SUMMARY\n\nFollowing the suppression-system discharge and evacuation, the planned Friday handover is suspended.\n\nOpen matters now include:\n- incident review by Operational Security;\n- confirmation of all personnel and restricted-area access;\n- completion of the archive reconciliation workstream;\n- completion of the terminal-network remediation workstream;\n- confirmation that essential server services remain stable.\n\nNo material is to be destroyed, transferred off Site or reclassified until the exception review is complete.\n\nMartin Webb, Project Manager:\n\"Friday's deadline has ceased to be the most important thing that happened on Friday.\"", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR47, 5U, "DR-47-RS-0043", "Operational Security Review Requirement", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T027, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nSITE CLOSURE PROJECT\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY REVIEW REQUIREMENT\n\nThe Site will remain under controlled closure pending a formal review of the suppression discharge.\n\nSecurity Office is to assemble:\n- access records;\n- visitor records;\n- attendance returns;\n- evacuation accountability;\n- duty communications;\n- CCTV coverage and relevant retained footage.\n\nThe Secretary's Office is to preserve Director correspondence, appointment material and incident-related incoming messages.\n\nThis review is fact-finding. No individual is to be identified as responsible solely because they were authorised to be present.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR47, 8U, "DR-47-RS-0080", "Remaining Workstream Release Authority", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T028, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nSITE CLOSURE PROJECT\nREMAINING WORKSTREAM RELEASE AUTHORITY\n\nThe closure suspension does not cancel the unfinished Records and Technology workstreams.\n\nOnce the initial safety state is confirmed, the Project Manager authorises both teams to resume the minimum work required to establish:\n1. the true custody state of final archive holdings; and\n2. the technical condition of the terminal/server route.\n\nAny work that may disturb incident-relevant equipment must be documented before continuation.\n\nThe previously deferred workstream is no longer to be held back for scheduling reasons.\n\nThere is no longer a Friday timetable to protect.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR47, 11U, "DR-47-RS-0117", "Incident Review Referral", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nSITE CLOSURE PROJECT\nINCIDENT REVIEW REFERRAL\n\nReferral to: Operational Security\nIncident: automatic Site evacuation following Halon discharge\nLocation of concern: Server Room / associated suppression controls\nInjury report: none at initial return\nFire report: not yet established\nCause: not established\n\nQuestions for review:\n- Was the discharge initiated by detection or manual release?\n- Who was authorised in the restricted area?\n- What maintenance or network work was under way?\n- Did any visitor or unauthorised person enter the relevant area?\n\nDo not answer the questions in the referral.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR47, 14U, "DR-47-RS-0152", "Closure Suspension Notice", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nSITE CLOSURE PROJECT\nCLOSURE SUSPENSION NOTICE\n\nEffective immediately, the planned building handover is paused.\n\nStaff required for incident review, archive custody, technical recovery and essential services may remain or return under Security direction. All other closure activity is suspended.\n\nTransfer vehicles are not to depart with the final archive batch.\nDecommissioning contractors are not to isolate further services.\nNo cabinet or cable-riser arrangement is to be tidied for appearance.\n\nPreserve the Site as found after evacuation, subject to life-safety requirements.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR47, 17U, "DR-47-RS-0187", "Revised Handover Conditions", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nSITE CLOSURE PROJECT\nREVISED HANDOVER CONDITIONS\n\nThe revised handover will require, in addition to the original closure controls:\n\n- completed incident chronology;\n- explanation of the suppression release input;\n- confirmation of personnel and visitor movements;\n- confirmation that archive exceptions are accounted for;\n- confirmation that server and backup services are stable;\n- Director approval after Security review.\n\nThe handover date is now \"when complete\".\n\nThis wording has been approved despite objections from the calendar.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR53, 2U, "DR-53-RS-0015", "Site Closure Direction", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T029, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nDIRECTOR'S OFFICE\nSITE CLOSURE DIRECTION\n\nThe Site is to close as part of the Department's approved centralisation programme.\n\nRecords functions will transfer to the central archive. Digital holdings will move to the consolidated service. Local administrative posts will be reassigned or concluded under existing personnel arrangements.\n\nThe closure is not a response to a security breach, disciplinary action or emergency condition.\n\nThe building is to be handed over only after archive custody, digital verification and essential safety controls are complete.\n\nSigned,\nDIRECTOR (HELEN CARTWRIGHT)\n\nDistribution: Project Manager, Senior Archivist, Facilities, Security, IT Support.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR53, 5U, "DR-53-RS-0052", "Executive Closure Briefing", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nDIRECTOR'S OFFICE\nEXECUTIVE CLOSURE BRIEFING\n\nPurpose:\nComplete an orderly transfer of the Site's remaining records and services before building handover.\n\nKnown pressure points:\n- final archive batch;\n- terminal-to-server verification route;\n- contractor sequencing;\n- restricted-area access during closure work.\n\nThe programme assumes routine operations until handover. Existing security and safety rules remain in force throughout.\n\nThe Director has specifically rejected any proposal to \"simplify\" closure by treating incomplete verification as post-handover work.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR53, 7U, "DR-53-RS-0078", "Centralisation Programme Summary", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nDIRECTOR'S OFFICE\nCENTRALISATION PROGRAMME SUMMARY\n\nThe Department is reducing small local records sites and consolidating holdings, specialist staff and computing services.\n\nExpected benefits:\n- fewer duplicate catalogues;\n- improved digital preservation;\n- central custody of high-classification holdings;\n- reduced building and support costs.\n\nKnown risks:\n- temporary workload increase during transfer;\n- overlap between physical and digital verification;\n- dependence on ageing local systems during the final weeks.\n\nThe Site closure forms one scheduled part of this programme. It is not an exceptional shutdown.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR53, 10U, "DR-53-RS-0115", "Director Annotation Record", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nDIRECTOR'S ANNOTATED COPY\nCLOSURE BRIEFING - MARGIN NOTES TRANSCRIBED\n\n\"Do not let the date become the objective.\"\n\n\"Records: I want signed custody, not 'everyone knows where the box is'.\"\n\n\"IT: keep the servers until verification is actually finished.\"\n\n\"Security: normal rules until the last person leaves.\"\n\n\"Facilities: confirm suppression system remains safe while contractors are in the building.\"\n\nFinal annotation beside Friday handover target:\n\"Only if true.\"", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR53, 12U, "DR-53-RS-0139", "Handover Authority Chain", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nDIRECTOR'S OFFICE\nHANDOVER AUTHORITY CHAIN\n\nOperational workstream owners certify completion to the Project Manager.\n\nThe Senior Archivist certifies archive custody and transfer readiness.\n\nIT Support certifies digital verification capability and final technical status.\n\nSecurity certifies access, incident and restricted-area exceptions.\n\nFacilities certifies building systems and decommissioning status.\n\nThe Project Manager assembles the closure certificate.\n\nThe Director alone releases the Site for handover.\n\nNo lower signature may substitute for a missing higher one, however attractively the empty box is initialled.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR53, 15U, "DR-53-RS-0165", "Final-Day Executive Diary Extract", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nDIRECTOR'S OFFICE\nFINAL-DAY DIARY EXTRACT\n\n08:15  Closure progress review.\n10:30  Central archive telephone update.\n12:00  Project Manager: two workstreams still open.\n13:45  Handover briefing moved to 16:00.\n14:25  Secretary notes interruption from Security duty call.\n14:30  Site evacuation; meeting abandoned.\n15:10  Initial accountability reported complete.\n15:25  Closure formally suspended.\n\nHandwritten below the final line:\n\"Ask what happened before asking who did it.\"", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_HR01, 2U, "HR-01-RS-0021", "Site Establishment Register", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T002, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nHUMAN RESOURCES\nSITE ESTABLISHMENT REGISTER\n\nAccommodation return: closure-period staffing.\\n\\nSite Director: Helen Cartwright.\n\nThe Main Office remains the administrative centre for the Site until final handover. Posts still requiring a physical desk are:\n\n- Project Manager: Martin Webb\n- Senior Archivist: Priya Patel\n- Records Officer: Daniel Price\n- IT Support: Claire Hughes\n- Facilities liaison: Imran Shah\n- Administrative support: Andrew Collins\n\nVacated posts and surplus furniture are excluded from the final-week allocation.\n\nHR instruction:\nDo not remove desk numbers until archive, technology and handover work is complete. Temporary moves must be recorded because staff location forms part of the final attendance and emergency-accountability return.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_HR01, 10U, "HR-01-RS-0107", "Main Office Staffing Allocation", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T003, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nHUMAN RESOURCES\nMAIN OFFICE STAFFING ALLOCATION\n\nFINAL WEEK - DESK PLAN\n\nDesk 01  Priya Patel - archive closure work\nDesk 02  Daniel Price - reconciliation support\nDesk 03  Andrew Collins - Administrative Support\nDesk 04  Claire Hughes  - temporary technical position\nDesk 05  Imran Shah - closure paperwork\nDesk 06  Martin Webb - handover control\n\nDesk 04 is temporary while the terminal cable fault is investigated. Staff may move for operational work, but the allocation remains the reference point for post, telephone and accountability.\n\nPlease leave the adhesive numbers in place. Facilities have already removed them once.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_HR01, 7U, "HR-01-RS-0082", "Organisational Chart", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nHUMAN RESOURCES\nSITE ORGANISATIONAL CHART - CLOSURE PERIOD\n\nHELEN CARTWRIGHT, DIRECTOR\n  |\n  |-- Priya Patel, SENIOR ARCHIVIST\n  |\n  |-- Rachel Morgan, SECURITY Manager  |\n  |-- Daniel Price, RECORDS OFFICER\n  |\n  |-- Claire Hughes, IT Manager\n  |\n  |-- Imran Shah, FACILITIES LIAISON\n  |\n  |-- Andrew Collins, ADMINISTRATIVE SUPPORT\n  |-- Martin Webb, PROJECT MANAGER\n\nOperational Security retains an independent duty line to the Director for access and incident matters.\n\nDuring closure, temporary tasking does not alter reporting responsibility. In particular, technical access remains an IT responsibility and archive release remains a Senior Archivist responsibility.\n\nThe chart replaces the earlier full-establishment version, which contained posts already transferred off Site.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_HR01, 11U, "HR-01-RS-0132", "Temporary Desk Reallocation Notice", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_HR01_DESK_REALLOCATION, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "FROM: Priya Patel\nTO: RECORDS OFFICER\nSUBJECT: TEMPORARY DESK REALLOCATION\n\nIT SUPPORT IS TO REMAIN AT DESK 04 UNTIL THE TERMINAL CABLE HAS BEEN REPLACED.\n\nTHE MUG AT DESK 01 IS NOT AN ARCHIVE ITEM AND SHOULD NOT BE ENTERED ON FORM AR-7.\n\nIF ANYONE MOVES MY IN-TRAY, IT WILL BECOME AN ARCHIVE ITEM OUT OF SPITE.\n\nSIGNED: Priya Patel, Senior Archivist", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_HR01, 12U, "HR-01-RS-0143", "Vacancy & Hot-Desk Provision", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nHUMAN RESOURCES\nVACANCY & HOT-DESK PROVISION\n\nSeveral posts have transferred ahead of Site closure. Their former desks may be used temporarily by closure staff, subject to the following:\n\n- retain the original desk number;\n- do not store classified material overnight;\n- leave a written allocation slip;\n- redirect calls through the current staff telephone list;\n- clear personal property before handover.\n\nDesk 04 is reserved for IT Support while the Main Office terminal fault remains open.\n\nA hot desk is still a desk. HR has been asked to make this explicit after an argument nobody wishes to document twice.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_HR01, 15U, "HR-01-RS-0180", "Staff Contact Directory", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nHUMAN RESOURCES\nSTAFF CONTACT DIRECTORY - FINAL WEEK\n\nHelen Cartwright, Director ................... Director's Office\nPriya Patel, Senior Archivist ................ Main Office, Desk 01 / Records Office\nDaniel Price, Records Officer ................ Main Office, Desk 02 / Records Office\nClaire Hughes, IT Manager .................... Main Office, Desk 04 / IT Support\nImran Shah, Facilities liaison ............... Main Office, Desk 05 / Facilities\nMartin Webb, Project Manager ................. Main Office, Desk 06\nRachel Morgan, Security Manager .............. Security Office\n\nInternal extensions remain in service until handover.\n\nFor emergency traffic use Security first. For closure scheduling use the Project Manager. For missing files use the Records Officer before using the word \"missing\" loudly.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_HR05, 2U, "HR-05-RS-0023", "Staff Welfare & Amenities Allocation", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T012, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nHUMAN RESOURCES\nSTAFF WELFARE & AMENITIES ALLOCATION\n\nThe Staff Room is to remain available throughout the final closure week.\n\nFacilities are to retain power to the refrigerator, kettle point and coffee equipment until the last staffed day. HR welfare materials and the noticeboard may remain in place until final housekeeping.\n\nNo archive material is to be stored in the Staff Room.\n\nPersonal food left after handover will be discarded without accession, cataloguing or ceremonial transfer.\n\nThe social committee has requested that this paragraph be read as a threat.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_HR05, 5U, "HR-05-RS-0050", "Shared Facilities Inventory", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nHUMAN RESOURCES\nSHARED FACILITIES INVENTORY\n\nStaff Room items retained to final day:\n\nRefrigerator .......... in service\nCoffee maker .......... in service\nMugs .................. assorted, ownership disputed\nBookcases ............. retain until clearance\nNoticeboard ........... retain closure notices\nFirst-aid guidance .... obsolete copy to be discarded\nUmbrella .............. owner unknown\nPaperback books ....... personal property unless claimed\n\nInventory excludes consumables.\n\nA cheese sandwich in the refrigerator is specifically not departmental property, despite having achieved a degree of permanence normally associated with fixtures.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_HR05, 8U, "HR-05-RS-0078", "Staff Room Cleaning Rota", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nHUMAN RESOURCES\nSTAFF ROOM CLEANING ROTA\n\nMONDAY       Andrew Collins\nTUESDAY      Daniel Price\nWEDNESDAY    Claire Hughes\nTHURSDAY     Imran Shah\nFRIDAY       Everyone, allegedly\n\nTasks:\n- wipe worktop;\n- empty bin;\n- rinse coffee pot;\n- remove expired milk;\n- leave noticeboard material until closure;\n- do not throw away labelled transfer paperwork carried in by mistake: return it to its owner.\n\nFriday note added in pencil:\n\"If the sandwich is still here, it wins.\"", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_HR05, 10U, "HR-05-RS-0106", "Tea & Coffee Contribution Note", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nHUMAN RESOURCES\nTEA & COFFEE CONTRIBUTION NOTE\n\nFinal-week contributions remain voluntary.\n\nTea: sufficient.\nCoffee: running low.\nSugar: inexplicably abundant.\nMilk: label bottles, particularly on Friday.\nBiscuits: no central provision.\n\nThe closure budget does not contain a line for \"morale caffeine\", despite several submissions.\n\nAny balance remaining in the tea tin after handover will be donated to the receiving office, provided the receiving office accepts coins sticky enough to qualify as heritage material.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_HR05, 13U, "HR-05-RS-0143", "Social Committee Circular", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nSOCIAL COMMITTEE CIRCULAR\n\nSUBJECT: LAST-DAY TEA, 15:30, STAFF ROOM\n\nAssuming the Site has not yet been handed over, evacuated, disconnected, flooded or absorbed into the central archive, staff are invited to a brief final tea.\n\nPlease sign the card on the noticeboard before Friday lunch.\n\nNo speeches longer than the kettle cycle.\nNo departmental records on the cake table.\nThe Project Manager has asked us not to call this \"the closure party\" until the Director has actually signed the closure.\n\nThis is probably wise.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_HR09, 2U, "HR-09-RS-0018", "Final Friday Attendance Return", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T043, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nHUMAN RESOURCES\nFINAL FRIDAY ATTENDANCE RETURN\n\nSigned present at start of duty:\n\nMartin Webb, Project Manager ............. PRESENT\nPriya Patel, Senior Archivist ............ PRESENT\nDaniel Price, Records Officer ............ PRESENT\nClaire Hughes, IT Manager ................ PRESENT\nImran Shah, Facilities liaison ........... PRESENT\nAndrew Collins, Administrative support ... PRESENT\n\nOperational Security duty staff are recorded on the separate Security rota.\n\nThe return confirms presence on Site. It does not establish where an individual was at any later minute.\n\nAmendments after evacuation must be countersigned and must not replace the original signed sheet.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_HR09, 5U, "HR-09-RS-0053", "Duty & Leave Status Schedule", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T044, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nHUMAN RESOURCES\nDUTY & LEAVE STATUS SCHEDULE\n\nFINAL FRIDAY\n\nPriya Patel:\nOn duty. Archive reconciliation and final verification.\n\nDaniel Price:\nOn duty. Records Office reconciliation and transfer staging.\n\nClaire Hughes:\nOn duty. Terminal network remediation and server-route checks.\n\nMartin Webb:\nOn duty. Closure coordination.\n\nImran Shah:\nOn duty. Decommissioning and retained services.\n\nNo listed member is recorded as annual leave, sick leave or external duty during the relevant closure window.\n\nSeparate movement records apply to restricted areas.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_HR09, 7U, "HR-09-RS-0066", "Final-Week Leave Summary", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nHUMAN RESOURCES\nFINAL-WEEK LEAVE SUMMARY\n\nMost routine leave was cleared before the final closure week.\n\nApproved leave affecting Site staffing:\n- two posts already transferred to Central Office;\n- one administrative half-day on Wednesday;\n- no leave recorded for Friday's archive, IT, facilities or project leads.\n\nManagers were instructed not to cancel pre-booked leave merely to make the building look busier.\n\nFor Friday, the closure team shown on the attendance return constitutes the expected staffed complement.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_HR09, 10U, "HR-09-RS-0103", "Overtime Authorisation", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nHUMAN RESOURCES\nOVERTIME AUTHORISATION\n\nAuthorised where required to complete closure tasks beyond normal hours:\n\nPriya Patel, Senior Archivist: archive transfer exceptions\nDaniel Price, Records Officer: reconciliation and transfer staging\nClaire Hughes, IT Manager: terminal/server remediation\nImran Shah, Facilities liaison: contractor and retained-service support\n\nMaximum: two hours without Project Manager extension.\n\nOvertime authorisation is not permission to bypass access controls, lone-working rules or equipment isolation.\n\nThe building may be closing. Employment law has not been notified.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_HR09, 12U, "HR-09-RS-0129", "Temporary Duty Allocation", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nHUMAN RESOURCES\nTEMPORARY DUTY ALLOCATION\n\nDuring the closure period:\n\nClaire Hughes may work from Main Office Desk 04 while tracing the terminal fault.\n\nThe Priya Patel may work between Main Office, Records Office and authorised verification locations.\n\nDaniel Price retains day-to-day control of the Records Office.\n\nFacilities staff may enter operational rooms for scheduled decommissioning subject to local access rules.\n\nTemporary location does not transfer responsibility for another officer's records, keys or equipment.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_HR09, 15U, "HR-09-RS-0166", "Attendance Amendment Register", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nHUMAN RESOURCES\nATTENDANCE AMENDMENT REGISTER\n\nFriday amendments:\n\n14:30 - Site evacuation. All persons marked OUT pending roll-call.\n15:10 - Security advises all closure staff accounted for.\n15:20 - Essential personnel permitted to remain available under Security direction.\n\nNo correction has been made to the original morning attendance signatures.\n\nReason:\nThe morning return answers \"who reported for duty?\" The evacuation sheet answers \"who was accounted for after the incident?\" Combining them would make both records less useful.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM04, 3U, "FM-04-RS-0035", "Facilities Access Authorisation", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T004, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nFACILITIES ACCESS AUTHORISATION\n\nThe Facilities Office remains operational for the duration of the closure programme.\n\nAuthorised users:\n- Imran Shah;\n- approved maintenance contractors under escort;\n- Martin Webb;\n- Security staff where required.\n\nThe room contains current maintenance schedules, service labels, plant references and decommissioning paperwork.\n\nDo not clear shelving until the final retained-services check has been signed.\n\nFacilities note:\nAnyone seeking a key should state which door it opens. \"The one down the corridor\" is no longer an acceptable asset description.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM04, 7U, "FM-04-RS-0072", "Internal Circulation Access Plan", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T005, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nINTERNAL CIRCULATION ACCESS PLAN\n\nClosure-period internal routes are to remain available between Reception, Main Office and the occupied support rooms.\n\nDoor plates are to remain fitted until handover so contractors and temporary staff can identify rooms without relying on memory.\n\nControlled rooms retain their normal access rules. Opening the corridor for closure traffic does not make restricted areas unrestricted.\n\nFacilities will remove surplus signage only after the Project Manager confirms that all final inspections are complete.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM04, 10U, "FM-04-RS-0104", "Site Directory Maintenance Note", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nSITE DIRECTORY MAINTENANCE NOTE\n\nThe corridor Site Directory has been amended to reflect closure-period room use.\n\nRemove:\n- offices already vacated;\n- obsolete team labels.\n\nRetain:\n- Reception;\n- Main Office;\n- Facilities;\n- Records Office;\n- IT Support;\n- Security Office;\n- Staff Room;\n- Server Room;\n- Director and Secretary accommodation.\n\nTemporary paper labels are acceptable where permanent plates have already been scheduled for removal.\n\nPlease stop correcting the map with pencil. Facilities owns a ruler.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM04, 14U, "FM-04-RS-0157", "Room Identification Schedule", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nROOM IDENTIFICATION SCHEDULE\n\nReception ............... Public arrival / visitor control\nMain Office ............. Closure administration\nFacilities .............. Maintenance and decommissioning\nRecords Office .......... Archive holdings and transfer staging\nIT Support .............. Local technology support\nSecurity Office ......... Access and incident control\nStaff Room .............. Welfare\nServer Room ............. Restricted technical services\nSecretary Office ........ Executive support\nDirector Office ......... Executive / handover authority\n\nRoom plates remain the authoritative local labels until physical handover.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM04, 17U, "FM-04-RS-0194", "Maintenance Responsibility Matrix", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nMAINTENANCE RESPONSIBILITY MATRIX\n\nLighting ................. Facilities\nPower distribution ....... Facilities / contractor\nSuppression equipment .... Facilities / specialist contractor\nTerminal equipment ....... IT Support\nNetwork cabling .......... IT Support\nServer hardware .......... IT Support\nSecure locks and keys .... Security\nArchive cabinets ......... Records / Security for access control\nFire routes .............. Facilities / Security\n\nCross-discipline work must identify an owner before it begins.\n\nThe cable riser is specifically marked as a shared work area: network cabling and suppression-control wiring occupy the same service route.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM04, 21U, "FM-04-RS-0236", "Final Week Work Order Summary", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nFINAL WEEK WORK ORDER SUMMARY\n\nOPEN:\n- remove surplus furniture labels;\n- inspect retained suppression controls;\n- support terminal cable remediation;\n- defer final service isolation until archive verification completes;\n- final corridor signage removal after handover.\n\nCLOSED:\n- redundant office lighting circuits;\n- non-essential storage clearance;\n- contractor welfare arrangements.\n\nHOLD:\n- Server Room services;\n- suppression system;\n- main archive terminal supply.\n\nHold items require explicit release. Closure does not mean \"switch off everything in alphabetical order.\"", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM07, 2U, "FM-07-RS-0013", "Final Decommissioning Schedule", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T008, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nFINAL DECOMMISSIONING SCHEDULE\n\nDecommissioning is sequenced after operational dependency, not room number.\n\nStage 1: surplus furniture and non-essential equipment.\nStage 2: vacated office services.\nStage 3: archive and IT equipment after verification.\nStage 4: retained life-safety and security systems at handover.\n\nThe Server Room, archive terminal, access control and suppression system remain operational until their owning workstreams release them.\n\nContractors are not to act on an old schedule where a HOLD label is present.\n\nA red tag beats a calendar.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM07, 5U, "FM-07-RS-0050", "Retained Services Schedule", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T009, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nRETAINED SERVICES SCHEDULE\n\nRETAIN THROUGH FINAL HANDOVER:\n- emergency lighting;\n- access control;\n- fire detection;\n- Halon suppression serving the Server Room;\n- Server Room power and ventilation;\n- archive terminal power;\n- essential network route;\n- internal telephone service.\n\nThe Halon system is deliberately retained because the Server Room remains live for backup and verification work.\n\nNo retained service is to be isolated merely because its surrounding office is otherwise ready for closure.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM07, 8U, "FM-07-RS-0085", "Asset Transfer Register", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nASSET TRANSFER REGISTER\n\nItems marked TRANSFER remain departmental property.\nItems marked DISPOSE may be removed only after local data, records and labels are cleared.\nItems marked RETAIN remain with the building until handover.\n\nServer, network and archive equipment are not to move until IT and Records release them.\n\nAsset labels must not be used as substitute packing tape.\n\nThe closure team has been reminded that an object may be obsolete, heavy and unpopular while still requiring a signature.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM07, 11U, "FM-07-RS-0120", "Utility Isolation Plan", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nUTILITY ISOLATION PLAN\n\nPlanned isolations follow completion of dependent work.\n\nDo not isolate:\n- Server Room power while final backup or verification remains open;\n- ventilation while the room is occupied;\n- suppression controls independently of the approved safety procedure;\n- telephone service before Security releases emergency communications.\n\nFacilities must record actual isolation time, not planned isolation time.\n\nBlank times on this form are preferable to invented punctuality.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM07, 14U, "FM-07-RS-0155", "Contractor Coordination Note", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nCONTRACTOR COORDINATION NOTE\n\nClosure contractors will encounter staff still working in rooms that appear otherwise vacant.\n\nBefore work:\n1. confirm room owner;\n2. check HOLD tags;\n3. identify shared cable or control routes;\n4. agree any isolation;\n5. record completion.\n\nParticular caution: Server Room cable-riser work shares space with suppression-control wiring.\n\nContractors are not authorised to disconnect labelled control wiring unless the work order expressly includes it.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM07, 17U, "FM-07-RS-0192", "Final Asset Sweep", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nFINAL ASSET SWEEP\n\nThe final sweep is to occur after operational work has ceased.\n\nCheck:\n- desks and drawers;\n- shelving;\n- equipment labels;\n- temporary work areas;\n- cable reels and tools;\n- transfer boxes;\n- keys and access cards.\n\nDo not remove items from an active incident or reconciliation area for tidiness.\n\nA neat empty room is not the objective. An accountable room is.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM13, 3U, "FM-13-RS-0047", "Suppression Control Panel Service Note", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_FM13_SUPPRESSION_SERVICE, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T006, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nSUPPRESSION CONTROL PANEL SERVICE NOTE\n\nLocation: Server Room cable-riser / suppression control\nStatus: retained in service through closure\n\nThe manual discharge circuit remains connected pending completion of cable-riser works. The control route shares the riser with network cabling.\n\nDuring Thursday maintenance, an intermittent input was observed while adjacent cabling was handled. No discharge command was confirmed and the panel returned to normal after the cable bundle was settled.\n\nAction:\nIsolate the manual release circuit before further intrusive riser work.\n\nFollow-up test deferred to Tuesday after the bank holiday unless closure activity requires earlier access.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM13, 6U, "FM-13-RS-0076", "Manual Discharge Circuit Test Record", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T007, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nMANUAL DISCHARGE CIRCUIT TEST RECORD\n\nContractor: Daniel Mercer\nCompany: Alderwick Fire & Safety Ltd.\n\nTest point: Main Office suppression control / Server Room release circuit.\n\nIndicator test: PASS\nContinuity: PASS\nManual input path: LIVE\nAutomatic detection path: PASS\nIsolation fitted for test: YES\nIsolation removed after test: YES\n\nObservation:\nMovement of the shared riser bundle produced a brief unstable reading on the manual-input monitor. Reading did not persist long enough to operate the release sequence during the test.\n\nRecommendation:\nIsolate before network cable replacement or any work likely to disturb the riser bundle.\n\nSigned: Daniel Mercer\nContract Engineer\nAlderwick Fire & Safety Ltd.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM13, 9U, "FM-13-RS-0110", "Suppression Zone Diagram Register", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nSUPPRESSION ZONE DIAGRAM REGISTER\n\nZone SR-1 covers the Server Room.\n\nAutomatic inputs:\n- fire detection loop;\n- confirmed alarm sequence.\n\nManual input:\n- discharge control circuit routed through the cable riser to the local release/control arrangement.\n\nOn discharge:\n- Halon release;\n- ventilation isolation;\n- local alarm;\n- Site evacuation response.\n\nDrawing note:\nNetwork services and the manual release circuit share part of the riser route. Maintain separation during cable work and isolate controls where separation cannot be assured.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM13, 12U, "FM-13-RS-0130", "Halon Cylinder Service Record", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nHALON CYLINDER SERVICE RECORD\n\nServer Room suppression cylinders inspected during closure maintenance.\n\nPressure: within service band.\nSeals: intact.\nActuation hardware: serviceable.\nReplacement due: after planned Site handover.\nStatus: RETAIN IN SERVICE.\n\nReason for retention:\nServer equipment remains powered for final backup and archive verification.\n\nThe system is not to be discharged for testing during closure. Manual circuit tests must use the approved electrical isolation.\n\nService label applied to cylinder bank and copied to Facilities file.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM13, 15U, "FM-13-RS-0167", "Alarm Loop Maintenance Note", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nALARM LOOP MAINTENANCE NOTE\n\nFire-detection loop checked following routine closure-period maintenance.\n\nNo persistent detector fault found.\nNo detector bypass left in place.\nServer Room detector indications normal.\nSuppression release circuit remains separately monitored.\n\nThe alarm loop and the manual release input are distinct paths. A release input can therefore be recorded without a preceding fire-detection condition.\n\nTechnicians are reminded not to describe every suppression activation as a \"fire alarm\" in maintenance paperwork.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM13, 18U, "FM-13-RS-0204", "Server Room Safety Inspection", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nSERVER ROOM SAFETY INSPECTION\n\nPre-closure inspection:\n\n[OK] Exit route clear\n[OK] Warning signage visible\n[OK] Ventilation operating\n[OK] Halon cylinders in service\n[OK] Detection loop normal\n[OK] Manual controls labelled\n[!] Cable-riser work remains open\n\nRestriction:\nAny intrusive work in the riser requires coordination between IT and Facilities because suppression-control wiring passes through the same area.\n\nInspection does not close the outstanding network work order.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM18, 2U, "FM-18-RS-0037", "Environmental Event Log", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T041, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nENVIRONMENTAL EVENT LOG\n\nFINAL FRIDAY\n\n14:28:41  Server Room temperature normal.\n14:28:44  Smoke detection: normal.\n14:28:46  Heat detection: normal.\n14:28:49  Suppression release sequence begins.\n14:28:50  Ventilation isolation commanded.\n14:28:52  Site alarm active.\n14:29:03  Server Room pressure event consistent with Halon discharge.\n\nNo preceding fire condition is recorded by the environmental system.\n\nThe log records sensor states and control events only. It does not identify the cause of the release input.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM18, 5U, "FM-18-RS-0074", "Fire Suppression Event Record", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T042, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nFIRE SUPPRESSION EVENT RECORD\n\nEvent: Server Room Halon discharge\nTime: approximately 14:29 Friday\n\nAutomatic fire criteria before release:\nSmoke detector ........ NO\nHeat detector ......... NO\nCombined fire state ... NO\n\nRelease input recorded:\nMANUAL RELEASE CHANNEL\n\nAutomatic responses:\nVentilation isolated.\nAlarm raised.\nEvacuation initiated.\n\nThe event record does not establish that a person operated a manual control. \"Manual channel\" identifies the electrical release path, not the hand that caused the signal.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM18, 7U, "FM-18-RS-0098", "Ventilation Isolation Sequence", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nVENTILATION ISOLATION SEQUENCE\n\nThe Server Room ventilation system is interlocked with suppression discharge.\n\nOn valid release:\n1. close supply damper;\n2. stop extract;\n3. confirm isolation;\n4. permit suppression sequence;\n5. maintain isolation until authorised reset.\n\nFriday event:\nIsolation command received and completed within expected interval.\n\nNo evidence of ventilation fault preceding the discharge.\n\nThe isolation performed as designed. The question lies upstream of it.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM18, 10U, "FM-18-RS-0135", "Environmental Sensor Summary", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nENVIRONMENTAL SENSOR SUMMARY\n\nReview period: 13:30-14:35 Friday.\n\nTemperature remained within normal operating range.\nNo smoke alarm was recorded.\nNo heat alarm was recorded.\nNo abnormal humidity event was recorded.\nVentilation status was normal until commanded to isolate during suppression.\n\nThe first abnormal event in the environmental sequence is the suppression release command.\n\nThis summary should be read with the suppression-control diagnostic, not as a standalone cause report.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM18, 12U, "FM-18-RS-0148", "Plant Response Timeline", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nPLANT RESPONSE TIMELINE\n\n14:28:49  Suppression release input accepted.\n14:28:50  Ventilation isolation begins.\n14:28:52  Local and Site alarms activate.\n14:28:57  Halon release confirmed.\n14:29:03  Environmental pressure change recorded.\n14:31:00  Facilities acknowledges plant alarm.\n14:36:00  Server Room access prohibited pending atmosphere check.\n\nAll automatic plant responses occurred in the expected order after the release input.\n\nNo plant action explains how that input arose.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM18, 15U, "FM-18-RS-0174", "Post-Incident Environmental Check", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nPOST-INCIDENT ENVIRONMENTAL CHECK\n\nServer Room entry permitted only after atmosphere confirmation.\n\nPost-event findings:\n- no fire damage observed;\n- no heat source identified;\n- ventilation equipment serviceable after reset;\n- Halon system discharged as designed;\n- cable-riser work area left in active-work condition;\n- control diagnostics retained for technical review.\n\nFacilities recommendation:\nDo not reset or reterminate the manual release circuit until IT and Security have documented the riser condition.\n\nThe room is safe to investigate, not safe to tidy.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_FM23, 0U, "FM-23-RS-0011", "Request for Preparation of Isometric Accommodation Plans", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T025, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nFACILITIES MANAGEMENT\nREQUEST FOR PREPARATION OF ISOMETRIC ACCOMMODATION PLANS\n\nTo: Drawing Office\nSubject: Closure-period Site plan\n\nPlease prepare an isometric accommodation plan from the current room schedule and corridor survey.\n\nPurpose:\nThe existing flat plan is adequate for floor area but poor at showing door relationships, furniture clearances and the relative position of service features during the handover walk-round.\n\nInclude only confirmed room boundaries and fixed or recorded major items. Do not infer concealed service routes.\n\nOne copy to Project Manager.\nOne copy to Facilities file.\n\nPencil perspective sketches are not to be filed as measured drawings, irrespective of confidence.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS07, 2U, "OS-07-RS-0024", "Final Week Visitor Access Register", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T030, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nFINAL WEEK VISITOR ACCESS REGISTER\n\nClosure-week visitor controls remain in force until the Director releases the Site.\n\nFriday entries:\n08:05  Archive transport liaison - Reception only - departed 08:27\n09:40  Facilities contractor - escorted - departed 11:15\n11:50  Central Office courier - Reception/Main Office - departed 12:08\n\nNo visitor entry is recorded after 12:08.\n\nNo visitor is recorded for the Server Room, Security Office or Records Office during the incident window.\n\nThis register records authorised sign-in. It should be checked against temporary-pass stubs and Security duty notes before any conclusion is drawn.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS07, 5U, "OS-07-RS-0061", "Contractor Access Authorisations", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T031, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nCONTRACTOR ACCESS AUTHORISATIONS\n\nFacilities contractor access for final-week works:\n\nPermitted:\n- Facilities Office;\n- agreed corridor routes;\n- non-restricted plant/service areas under escort.\n\nNot permitted without separate authority:\n- Records Office;\n- Security Office;\n- Server Room;\n- secure cabinets;\n- archive transfer material.\n\nFriday contractor activity concluded before midday.\n\nThe contractor's temporary pass was returned at Reception. No extension into the afternoon incident period is recorded.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS07, 8U, "OS-07-RS-0098", "Temporary Pass Reconciliation", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nTEMPORARY PASS RECONCILIATION\n\nPass issue and return check, Friday:\n\nPass V-12 ........ issued 08:05 / returned 08:27\nPass C-04 ........ issued 09:40 / returned 11:15\nPass C-07 ........ issued 11:50 / returned 12:08\n\nOutstanding visitor passes at 14:00: NONE.\n\nA returned pass does not prove that every movement was observed. It does establish that no active visitor credential remained issued through Reception at the relevant time.\n\nReception carbon copies agree with the Security pass sheet.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS07, 11U, "OS-07-RS-0135", "Reception Visitor Summary", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nRECEPTION VISITOR SUMMARY\n\nThe Site received three external visitors on Friday before lunch.\n\nAll were expected.\nAll were signed in.\nAll were assigned a host or escort where required.\nAll were recorded as departed before 12:10.\n\nNo late arrival, unscheduled delivery or replacement pass was recorded between 12:10 and the evacuation.\n\nSecurity review note:\nThe absence of an unexplained visitor narrows the access picture. It does not establish what authorised staff did.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS07, 14U, "OS-07-RS-0170", "Restricted Visitor Escort Note", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nRESTRICTED VISITOR ESCORT NOTE\n\nVisitors must not be left unescorted in routes giving access to restricted rooms.\n\nWhere a contractor requires work near a restricted boundary, the escort is to record:\n- purpose;\n- room or route;\n- arrival and departure;\n- any additional key or pass issued.\n\nNo Friday visitor escort entry identifies Server Room access.\n\nA Facilities contractor worked on closure tasks in the morning but was signed out before the afternoon incident period.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS07, 17U, "OS-07-RS-0205", "Visitor Badge Return Register", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nVISITOR BADGE RETURN REGISTER\n\nFinal-week temporary badges are to be returned at Reception and counted at close of duty.\n\nFriday pre-evacuation count:\nIssued today: 3\nReturned today: 3\nPreviously issued and still active: 0\nUnaccounted badges: 0\n\nOne spare lanyard was found in the Reception desk drawer and has never been numbered or issued.\n\nDo not promote spare stationery into a security incident simply because it has a clip.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS18, 0U, "OS-18-RS-0007", "Temporary Restricted Area Authorisation", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T033, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nTEMPORARY RESTRICTED AREA AUTHORISATION\n\nHolder: Priya Patel, Senior Archivist\nArea: Server Room\nPeriod: final closure week only\nPurpose: archive verification and final transfer checks requiring comparison with server-held records.\n\nConditions:\n- access limited to verification activity;\n- coordinate technical work with IT Support;\n- no alteration to server or suppression equipment;\n- return authority on completion of closure.\n\nApproved by: Security Officer\nNoted by: Martin Webb, Project Manager\n\nThis authority supplements normal archive duties. It does not grant general technical-control privileges.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS18, 1U, "OS-18-RS-0022", "Restricted Area Access Matrix", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T032, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nRESTRICTED AREA ACCESS MATRIX\n\nSERVER ROOM\n\nIT Support ................. STANDING ACCESS\nSecurity Duty Officer ...... STANDING ACCESS\nFacilities engineer ........ CONTROLLED / MAINTENANCE\nSenior Archivist ........... TEMPORARY AUTHORISATION - FINAL WEEK\nRecords Officer ............ NO ROUTINE ACCESS\nGeneral closure staff ...... NO ACCESS\nVisitors/contractors ....... ESCORT + SPECIFIC AUTHORITY\n\nThe matrix records who may enter, not who did enter.\n\nFriday movement evidence must be read with duty logs, attendance records and the temporary-authorisation sheet.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS26, 2U, "OS-26-RS-0027", "Initial Halon Incident Report", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T034, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nINITIAL HALON INCIDENT REPORT\n\nDate: Final Friday\nTime notified: approximately 14:29\nLocation: Server Room\n\nThe Site alarm followed a suppression-system discharge in the Server Room. No preceding report of smoke or fire was received by Security.\n\nImmediate actions:\n- evacuate Site;\n- prohibit Server Room re-entry;\n- conduct roll-call;\n- notify Facilities and Director;\n- preserve access and incident records.\n\nCause at time of report: UNKNOWN.\n\nThe report is intentionally preliminary. Do not amend \"unknown\" merely because a later explanation appears plausible.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS26, 5U, "OS-26-RS-0064", "Evacuation Accountability Return", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T035, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nEVACUATION ACCOUNTABILITY RETURN\n\nRoll-call completed after Friday suppression incident.\n\nMartin Webb, Project Manager .............. accounted for\nPriya Patel, Senior Archivist ............. accounted for\nDaniel Price, Records Officer ............. accounted for\nClaire Hughes, IT Manager ................. accounted for\nImran Shah, Facilities liaison ............ accounted for\nAndrew Collins, Administrative support .... accounted for\nRachel Morgan, Security Manager ........... accounted for\n\nVisitors on Site at alarm: NONE RECORDED\nUnaccounted persons: NONE\nInjuries reported: NONE\n\nThe Senior Archivist and IT Support were reported from the restricted-area side of the Site during evacuation and were accounted for safely.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS26, 8U, "OS-26-RS-0101", "Restricted Area Evacuation Note", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T036, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nRESTRICTED AREA EVACUATION NOTE\n\nSecurity sweep information indicates that two authorised staff were working in or immediately around the Server Room route before the alarm:\n\n- Claire Hughes, IT Manager, conducting network remediation;\n- Priya Patel, Senior Archivist, attending for final verification work.\n\nBoth held valid access at the time.\nBoth evacuated safely.\nNeither is identified by this note as having operated suppression equipment.\n\nThe Server Room was not re-entered until atmosphere and safety checks were complete.\n\nPreserve the access matrix and temporary authorisation with this note.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS26, 11U, "OS-26-RS-0138", "Incident Timeline Worksheet", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nINCIDENT TIMELINE WORKSHEET\n\n14:20-14:28  Technical and verification work continues in restricted area.\n14:28:49        Suppression system accepts release input.\n14:28-14:29     Alarm and ventilation isolation sequence.\n14:29            Site evacuation begins.\n14:31            Security begins roll-call.\n15:10            All expected personnel accounted for.\n15:20            Initial no-injury status confirmed.\n\nOpen questions:\n- source of release input;\n- exact work being performed at the cable riser;\n- whether control wiring was disturbed;\n- whether any unrecorded access occurred.\n\nDo not convert questions into findings.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS26, 13U, "OS-26-RS-0158", "Post-Evacuation Site Check", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nPOST-EVACUATION SITE CHECK\n\nFollowing atmosphere clearance, Security and Facilities conducted a limited preservation check.\n\nObserved:\n- no fire damage in Server Room;\n- cable-riser work left incomplete;\n- tools and pulled network cable present;\n- suppression equipment discharged;\n- relevant panels and paperwork left in place;\n- no obvious forced entry to restricted rooms.\n\nNothing was repositioned except where required for safety.\n\nThe area was then held for technical examination.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS26, 16U, "OS-26-RS-0192", "Emergency Services Contact Note", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nEMERGENCY SERVICES CONTACT NOTE\n\n14:31  Internal alarm acknowledged by Security.\n14:33  Facilities confirms Halon discharge indication.\n14:35  External emergency advice line contacted.\n14:39  No fire condition reported; room remains sealed pending atmosphere check.\n14:48  Advice received: maintain exclusion until safe concentration confirmed.\n15:02  Facilities begins controlled ventilation/re-entry procedure.\n\nNo external firefighting action was required.\n\nThe absence of fire response does not diminish the seriousness of an accidental suppression discharge.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS26, 19U, "OS-26-RS-0215", "No-Injury Confirmation", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nNO-INJURY CONFIRMATION\n\nFollowing the Server Room Halon discharge and Site evacuation:\n\nFatalities: NONE\nReported injuries: NONE\nMedical treatment required: NONE\nUnaccounted personnel: NONE\n\nAll staff present at the start of the evacuation were accounted for.\n\nThe incident remains reportable because of the suppression discharge, evacuation and potential exposure risk.\n\nThis form addresses people, not cause. Technical investigation remains open.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS34, 2U, "OS-34-RS-0029", "Security Memo: Master Cabinet Register Control", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T037, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nSECURITY MEMO: MASTER CABINET REGISTER CONTROL\n\nSecure-cabinet access codes are controlled as records in their own right.\n\nThe current master register is held in the Security secure cabinet. It lists the valid code for each controlled cabinet and records the date of the last change.\n\nThe Security cabinet's own code is not to appear on desk copies, door labels or routine cabinet sheets. The authorised reference is held separately under Director-controlled procedure.\n\nWhen using a recovered copy, verify the cabinet identifier before relying on the number.\n\nA correct code for the wrong cabinet remains wrong in every useful sense.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS34, 5U, "OS-34-RS-0066", "Secure Storage Access Procedure", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T038, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nSECURE STORAGE ACCESS PROCEDURE\n\nBefore opening a secure cabinet:\n\n1. Confirm the cabinet identifier.\n2. Confirm your authority to access its contents.\n3. Obtain the current code from the approved register or authorised holder.\n4. Enter the code without leaving it written at the cabinet.\n5. Relock after use.\n6. Record access where the cabinet register requires it.\n\nCodes are cabinet-specific and may be changed independently.\n\nDo not test remembered numbers across several cabinets. Security calls this \"guessing\" even when the person guessing feels strongly about it.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS34, 8U, "OS-34-RS-0094", "Key Safe Custody Note", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nKEY SAFE CUSTODY NOTE\n\nPhysical keys and combination-controlled storage are administered separately.\n\nThe complete Site key set remains in the Security key cabinet until handover. Keys removed for closure work must be signed out and returned before the end of duty.\n\nA key does not substitute for a cabinet combination where both controls are fitted.\n\nSpare and obsolete keys are to be tagged rather than tested experimentally against every lock in the building.\n\nThe final key count is part of building handover.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS34, 10U, "OS-34-RS-0112", "Master Cabinet Register Recovery Note", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nMASTER CABINET REGISTER RECOVERY NOTE\n\nThe closure file confirms that the master secure-cabinet register was still active on the final Friday.\n\nNo scheduled bulk code change occurred before the incident.\nNo cabinet was authorised to use a shared \"closure code\".\nIndividual cabinet codes remained in force.\n\nSecurity retained the master register for final reconciliation and handover.\n\nIf a local note disagrees with the master register, treat the local note as superseded unless its change is separately authorised.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS34, 13U, "OS-34-RS-0140", "Secure Cabinet Code Handling", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nSECURE CABINET CODE HANDLING\n\nCode-handling reminders for closure staff:\n\n- never write a code on the cabinet;\n- never include a code in an unclassified handover checklist;\n- never reuse a room number as a code;\n- destroy superseded working slips;\n- report a suspected disclosure before changing anything;\n- record the authorised change afterward.\n\nClosure work creates more temporary paperwork than usual. It does not create a holiday from key control.\n\nSecurity will provide current codes to authorised staff on request.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS41, 0U, "OS-41-RS-0003", "Final-Day Duty Communications Log", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T039, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nFINAL-DAY DUTY COMMUNICATIONS LOG\n\n13:52  IT Support advises Main Office terminal fault traced beyond local desk connection.\n14:03  IT Support proceeding to check Server Room route.\n14:08  Senior Archivist requests access confirmation for final verification activity.\n14:11  Security confirms temporary authorisation remains valid.\n14:18  Facilities queried regarding cable-riser suppression isolation.\n14:21  Facilities advises service note applies; engineer not yet present at riser.\n14:29  Site alarm / suppression event.\n14:31  Evacuation roll-call opened.\n\nNo visitor or unexplained access call is recorded during this period.\n\nLog compiled from duty telephone sheet; timings are operator entries, not automated timestamps.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS48, 2U, "OS-48-RS-0036", "CCTV Coverage & Retention Index", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T040, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nCCTV COVERAGE & RETENTION INDEX\n\nActive closure-period cameras cover:\n\nCAM 1  Reception entrance\nCAM 2  Reception desk / lobby\nCAM 3  Main corridor west\nCAM 4  IT Support entrance\nCAM 5  Records Office entrance\nCAM 6  Security approach\n\nNo camera covers the interior of the Server Room.\nNo camera covers the cable riser.\nRestricted-room interiors were deliberately excluded from routine CCTV coverage.\n\nRetention: standard rolling period unless marked for incident preservation.\n\nCoverage can show approach and entry. It cannot show what occurred beyond the protected door.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS48, 5U, "OS-48-RS-0073", "IT Support Entrance Event Summary", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nIT SUPPORT ENTRANCE EVENT SUMMARY\n\nCAM 4 - Friday incident window\n\n13:47  IT Support enters.\n13:55  IT Support exits carrying cable tester.\n14:02  IT Support re-enters.\n14:17  Senior Archivist passes corridor toward restricted-area route.\n14:29  Alarm condition; staff movement toward exits.\n14:32  Corridor cleared.\n\nNo visitor or unknown person is recorded entering IT Support during the reviewed interval.\n\nCamera 4 does not view the Server Room interior and cannot establish activity at the cable riser.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS48, 7U, "OS-48-RS-0086", "Camera Coverage Diagram", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nCAMERA COVERAGE DIAGRAM - TEXT REGISTER\n\nReception cameras observe public arrival.\nCorridor cameras observe approaches to office doors.\nIT Support camera observes the room entrance and immediate corridor.\nRecords camera observes the Records Office entrance.\nSecurity approach is covered separately.\n\nDeliberate blind areas:\n- office interiors;\n- secure cabinet contents;\n- Server Room interior;\n- service risers.\n\nBlind areas are privacy/security design choices, not camera failures.\n\nUse access records where CCTV coverage ends.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS48, 10U, "OS-48-RS-0112", "Retention Schedule", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nCCTV RETENTION SCHEDULE\n\nNormal footage:\nRolling retention under standard Site schedule.\n\nIncident-marked footage:\nPreserve immediately and remove from automatic overwrite cycle.\n\nFriday channels marked for preservation:\nReception\nMain corridor\nIT Support entrance\nRecords Office entrance\nSecurity approach\n\nNo Server Room interior footage exists because no camera was installed there.\n\nA retention request cannot preserve a view that was never recorded.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS48, 12U, "OS-48-RS-0136", "Monitor Bank Channel Register", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nMONITOR BANK CHANNEL REGISTER\n\n1  Reception Entrance\n2  Reception Desk\n3  Main Corridor\n4  IT Support Entrance\n5  Records Office Entrance\n6  Security Approach\n7  Spare / no signal\n8  Spare / test\n\nChannel 4 label renewed during closure work.\nChannel 7 intermittent snow is an unused input, not a hidden camera.\n\nThe monitor bank selector corresponds to this register.\n\nSecurity staff are reminded to record channel number when noting an event.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_OS48, 15U, "OS-48-RS-0173", "Final-Day CCTV Review Note", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nOPERATIONAL SECURITY\nFINAL-DAY CCTV REVIEW NOTE\n\nReviewed period: 13:30 to evacuation.\n\nObserved movements are consistent with expected closure staffing:\n- Claire Hughes moving between Main Office/IT Support and the restricted-area route;\n- Priya Patel proceeding toward authorised verification work;\n- no unexplained visitor arrival;\n- no unidentified person entering the IT Support approach.\n\nLimit:\nCCTV does not show the Server Room interior or cable-riser work.\n\nConclusion:\nThe footage supports the access chronology but cannot determine the physical cause of the suppression release.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS02, 2U, "TS-02-RS-0017", "Office Terminal Connectivity Fault Report", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T019, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nOFFICE TERMINAL CONNECTIVITY FAULT REPORT\n\nAsset: Main Office archive terminal\nReported: Final Thursday\nStatus: terminal operational / network service unavailable\n\nLocal power-on test is satisfactory. Keyboard, display and local diagnostic routine complete normally. Link indication is absent at the desk network connection.\n\nInitial action:\n- retain terminal in place;\n- replace local lead for test;\n- compare with diagnostic card;\n- trace service upstream if link remains absent.\n\nDo not exchange the terminal until the network path has been tested. The machine is old, not automatically guilty.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS02, 5U, "TS-02-RS-0052", "Local Terminal Diagnostic Result", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T020, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nLOCAL TERMINAL DIAGNOSTIC RESULT\n\nMain Office archive terminal.\n\nSelf-test ............... PASS\nLocal storage ........... PASS\nDisplay ................. PASS\nKeyboard ................ PASS\nNetwork interface ....... PASS\nDesk link ............... NO CARRIER\n\nA known-good short lead produces the same result at the desk outlet.\n\nFinding:\nThe terminal is serviceable. The fault lies beyond the local machine or at the building network path.\n\nNext action:\nCheck IT Support patch panel and onward route before changing terminal hardware.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS02, 8U, "TS-02-RS-0087", "Temporary Workstation Note", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nTEMPORARY WORKSTATION NOTE\n\nIT Support will work from Main Office Desk 04 while the archive terminal fault remains open.\n\nReason:\nThe affected terminal must remain available for repeated link tests and closure staff require immediate support.\n\nTemporary equipment at Desk 04:\n- cable tester;\n- diagnostic card;\n- spare patch leads;\n- terminal-status printouts.\n\nDo not relocate the test kit to IT Support without leaving a note. The last two hours of Thursday were spent looking for the cable tester because somebody had put it away properly.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS02, 11U, "TS-02-RS-0122", "Network Lead Test", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nNETWORK LEAD TEST\n\nDesk lead removed and tested.\n\nPair continuity: PASS\nConnector condition: serviceable\nSubstitute lead test: no change to fault\nLocal terminal interface: serviceable\n\nConclusion:\nThe loose lead between terminal and desk outlet is not the cause of the missing network service.\n\nLead returned to desk for identification purposes.\n\nEscalate to fixed route and patch-panel checks.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS02, 14U, "TS-02-RS-0159", "Terminal Hardware Check", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nTERMINAL HARDWARE CHECK\n\nArchive terminal opened for closure-period hardware inspection.\n\nNo failed board indicators.\nNo overheated component.\nNetwork interface seated correctly.\nLocal diagnostic routine repeats cleanly.\nClock discrepancy within known tolerance.\nDust level classified as \"historic but non-operational\".\n\nNo hardware replacement recommended.\n\nThe continuing network fault should be investigated as infrastructure.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS02, 17U, "TS-02-RS-0196", "Escalation to Infrastructure", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nESCALATION TO INFRASTRUCTURE\n\nThe Main Office terminal fault is transferred from endpoint support to network infrastructure.\n\nEvidence from local checks:\n- terminal powers and self-tests correctly;\n- network interface reports healthy;\n- local patch lead tests correctly;\n- service remains absent at the desk outlet.\n\nRequired:\nTrace the assigned circuit at the IT Support patch panel and verify continuity toward the Server Room distribution route.\n\nClosure impact:\nDigital holdings verification remains blocked until connectivity is restored.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS06, 3U, "TS-06-RS-0035", "Terminal Network Cable Route Investigation", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T021, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nTERMINAL NETWORK CABLE ROUTE INVESTIGATION\n\nCircuit: Main Office archive terminal\n\nIT Support patch-panel records identify the office outlet and its onward route toward the Server Room distribution point.\n\nThe local patch position is correctly labelled and connected. No cross-patch or retired-port error was found.\n\nThe route continues through the Server Room cable riser, where closure-period cable work is already scheduled.\n\nAction:\nPerform continuity tests from both ends before replacing the fixed run.\n\nNote:\nThe riser also contains non-network control cabling. Observe Facilities isolation requirements before disturbing bundles.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS06, 6U, "TS-06-RS-0058", "Distribution Panel Test Record", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T022, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nDISTRIBUTION PANEL TEST RECORD\n\nMain Office archive circuit.\n\nIT Support panel port: signal path present to intermediate point.\nServer-side route: intermittent/open under movement.\nPatch lead substitution: no improvement.\nPort re-seat: no lasting improvement.\n\nThe fault appears to be on the fixed route between IT Support and the Server Room termination rather than at either active device.\n\nCable-riser access is required.\n\nFacilities to be notified before intrusive work because the riser carries suppression-control wiring in addition to network services.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS06, 9U, "TS-06-RS-0092", "Patch Panel Port Schedule", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nPATCH PANEL PORT SCHEDULE\n\nMAIN OFFICE ARCHIVE TERMINAL\nDesk outlet: MO-T04\nIT Support panel: P2-17\nServer route: SR-RISER / N-17\nService: archive verification network\nStatus: FAULT OPEN\n\nAdjacent positions:\nP2-16 general office\nP2-18 spare\nP2-19 retired\n\nHandwritten correction:\n\"17, not 19. The faded label is older than the person reading it.\"\n\nRetired labels are to remain struck through until final cable removal so they cannot be mistaken for live routes.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS06, 12U, "TS-06-RS-0129", "Server Route Identification", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nSERVER ROUTE IDENTIFICATION\n\nThe affected archive-terminal circuit enters the Server Room via the shared cable riser and terminates at the distribution side of the server network.\n\nThe riser contains:\n- network copper;\n- legacy telephone pairs;\n- suppression manual-release/control wiring;\n- service labels from previous modifications.\n\nThe network route can be worked without altering suppression equipment, but the cable bundle is physically close.\n\nFacilities isolation must be confirmed before pulling, rethreading or separating cables in the riser.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS06, 15U, "TS-06-RS-0166", "Cable Continuity Test", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nCABLE CONTINUITY TEST\n\nCircuit N-17.\n\nStatic test: intermittent continuity failure.\nFlex test at IT Support end: no change.\nFlex test at Server Room riser: fault changes state.\nConnector terminations: visually serviceable.\nCable jacket near riser: compressed among older control wiring.\n\nFinding:\nFault localised to the riser section.\n\nProposed action:\nFree the affected network cable, inspect damage and replace the local section if required.\n\nSafety condition:\nConfirm isolation status of adjacent suppression-control circuit before disturbing the bundle.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS06, 18U, "TS-06-RS-0203", "Network Remediation Work Order", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nNETWORK REMEDIATION WORK ORDER\n\nWork order: restore Main Office archive-terminal route.\n\nTasks:\n1. Obtain Server Room access.\n2. Confirm Facilities control-circuit isolation.\n3. Photograph or sketch cable-riser condition.\n4. Free network circuit N-17 from compressed bundle.\n5. Replace damaged section as necessary.\n6. Test end-to-end.\n7. Restore digital verification service.\n8. Record any unexpected wiring interaction.\n\nFriday note:\nWork commenced pending Facilities attendance. Full circuit isolation confirmation not yet signed at time of last entry.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS08, 2U, "TS-08-RS-0026", "Historical Terminal Fault 1", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nHISTORICAL TERMINAL FAULT 1\n\nPrevious incident: archive terminal intermittently lost network service after furniture movement.\n\nCause:\nDesk patch lead partially unseated.\n\nResolution:\nConnector reseated and retaining clip replaced.\n\nRelevance to current fault:\nLow. The present desk lead and terminal interface have both passed test.\n\nFiled for trend comparison because the same symptom has previously had a much simpler cause.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS08, 4U, "TS-08-RS-0047", "Historical Terminal Fault 2", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nHISTORICAL TERMINAL FAULT 2\n\nPrevious incident: archive terminal displayed \"host unavailable\" for approximately 40 minutes.\n\nCause:\nServer maintenance overran.\n\nTerminal hardware was not at fault.\n\nResolution:\nService restored when server returned.\n\nRelevance to current fault:\nThe present server remains available to other services, making a general server outage unlikely.\n\nSupport note:\nIdentical messages can have different causes. This is why we test things.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS08, 7U, "TS-08-RS-0084", "Legacy Patch Workaround", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nLEGACY PATCH WORKAROUND\n\nAn earlier office rearrangement left one network route using an intermediate patch position that is no longer shown clearly on the wall label.\n\nTemporary workaround was documented pending a full recable that never became sufficiently urgent to fund.\n\nThe archive-terminal circuit does not use that retired position, but the nearby labels remain confusing.\n\nClosure action:\nRemove obsolete labels only after all live circuits have been positively identified.\n\nIT Support note:\n\"Temporary\" has survived three office managers and one budget cycle.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS08, 9U, "TS-08-RS-0105", "Support Trend Summary", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nSUPPORT TREND SUMMARY\n\nArchive-terminal faults over the previous two years fall into three categories:\n\nLocal lead/connector ........ several minor incidents\nServer availability ......... two planned/known incidents\nFixed building route ........ rare\n\nCurrent case differs from the common local faults:\nthe endpoint is healthy and the fixed route shows movement-sensitive continuity at the Server Room riser.\n\nHistorical frequency should inform diagnosis, not override current test results.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS10, 2U, "TS-10-RS-0031", "Final Digital Holdings Verification Report", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T023, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nFINAL DIGITAL HOLDINGS VERIFICATION REPORT\n\nStatus: NOT COMPLETED\n\nVerification media and checksum lists have been prepared. The Main Office archive terminal cannot currently reach the server holdings because of the open network-route fault.\n\nCompleted:\n- verification set identified;\n- media prepared;\n- expected checksums printed;\n- transfer labels prepared.\n\nOutstanding:\n- live comparison against server holdings;\n- exception resolution;\n- Senior Archivist confirmation.\n\nNo discrepancy in the holdings is asserted at this stage. The verification has not run.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS10, 5U, "TS-10-RS-0068", "Verification Media Preparation Record", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T024, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nVERIFICATION MEDIA PREPARATION RECORD\n\nTransfer verification set prepared for final archive handover.\n\nMedia case sealed for working custody but not final transfer.\nChecksum printout enclosed separately.\nSpare media retained in IT Support.\nArchive-transfer labels prepared.\nSenior Archivist review required after successful comparison.\n\nThe prepared media must not be overwritten while the network fault remains unresolved.\n\nPrepared is not verified.\nLabelled is not transferred.\nFriday is not yet finished.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS10, 8U, "TS-10-RS-0103", "Checksum Preparation Sheet", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nCHECKSUM PREPARATION SHEET\n\nExpected checksum list generated from the last confirmed server index before final verification.\n\nPurpose:\nDetect missing, altered or duplicated digital holdings during the closure comparison.\n\nThe sheet is a reference set only. It does not prove the current server state until the live comparison is completed.\n\nAny mismatch is to be recorded before corrective action so the original condition remains auditable.\n\nDo not manually \"correct\" a checksum because the filename looks right.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS10, 11U, "TS-10-RS-0138", "Archive Transfer Media List", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nARCHIVE TRANSFER MEDIA LIST\n\nFinal verification case contains:\n\nMedia A  catalogue export\nMedia B  document-index copy\nMedia C  closure-period change set\nMedia D  verification utilities\nPrinted checksum sheet\nTransfer labels\n\nSpare media wallet remains in IT Support and is not part of the transfer set.\n\nFinal seal is to be applied only after live verification and Priya Patel, Senior Archivist sign-off.\n\nThe case is ready to use, not ready to leave.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS10, 14U, "TS-10-RS-0173", "Verification Blocker Note", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nVERIFICATION BLOCKER NOTE\n\nBlocker: Main Office archive terminal cannot reach server holdings.\n\nEndpoint checks: PASS\nIT Support patching: PASS to intermediate route\nFixed circuit: fault localised toward Server Room cable riser\n\nImpact:\nFinal digital holdings comparison cannot proceed.\nPhysical transfer batch remains awaiting paired verification.\nSenior Archivist cannot sign final archive release.\n\nOwner: IT Support\nDependency: network remediation work order.\n\nWorkaround rejected:\nUsing an unverified older copy would satisfy the timetable, not the control.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS10, 17U, "TS-10-RS-0210", "Digital Holdings Handover Checklist", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nDIGITAL HOLDINGS HANDOVER CHECKLIST\n\n[OK] Verification media prepared\n[OK] Expected checksum set printed\n[OK] Transfer labels prepared\n[  ] Network route restored\n[  ] Live server comparison complete\n[  ] Differences resolved\n[  ] Senior Archivist review\n[  ] Final media seal\n[  ] Handover receipt\n\nStatus: HOLD\n\nDo not initial future work in advance.\n\nThis instruction was added after somebody described empty boxes as \"administrative latency\".", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS14, 2U, "TS-14-RS-0011", "Server Availability & Backup Operations Summary", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T045, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nSERVER AVAILABILITY & BACKUP OPERATIONS SUMMARY\n\nThe Server Room remains operational through final Site closure.\n\nReason:\n- final backup rotation;\n- archive holdings verification;\n- transfer preparation;\n- controlled shutdown after acceptance.\n\nServer services were not scheduled for early removal or power isolation.\n\nAccess remains restricted under the normal matrix.\n\nTechnology Services will release the room to Facilities only after backup and verification dependencies are closed.\n\nThe building may be nearly empty. The servers are still working.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS14, 5U, "TS-14-RS-0048", "Final Backup Window Schedule", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T046, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nFINAL BACKUP WINDOW SCHEDULE\n\nThursday 18:00  routine incremental\nFriday 07:00    final pre-handover backup\nFriday 13:00    verification snapshot\nFriday 16:00    contingency copy if handover delayed\n\nFriday 07:00 backup completed.\n13:00 snapshot completed with server services available.\n\nAny incident after the snapshot requires Technology Services to decide whether a further copy is necessary before shutdown.\n\nBackup completion does not replace archive verification. They protect different risks.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS14, 8U, "TS-14-RS-0085", "Archive Verification Dependency Note", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T047, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nARCHIVE VERIFICATION DEPENDENCY NOTE\n\nFinal archive verification depends on:\n\n1. server holdings remaining online;\n2. the Main Office terminal route being restored;\n3. prepared verification media remaining unchanged;\n4. Senior Archivist access for sign-off.\n\nThe server side is available.\nThe network path remains the blocking dependency.\n\nDo not shut down the server merely because the office terminal cannot currently reach it.\n\nA road closure does not prove the destination has vanished.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS14, 11U, "TS-14-RS-0120", "Backup Rotation Log", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nBACKUP ROTATION LOG\n\nTHU 18:00  Incremental set B7 ........ COMPLETE\nFRI 07:00  Final full set C1 ......... COMPLETE\nFRI 13:00  Verification snapshot C1-V  COMPLETE\n\nMedia C1 retained in Server Room backup case pending handover.\nPrevious rotation retained until final acceptance.\n\nNo failed backup is recorded in the relevant period.\n\nOperator note at 13:12:\n\"Server fine. Network route still not fine. These are separate facts.\"", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS14, 14U, "TS-14-RS-0155", "Server Availability Checklist", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nSERVER AVAILABILITY CHECKLIST\n\n[OK] Core services running\n[OK] Archive holdings accessible locally\n[OK] Storage health normal\n[OK] Backup completed\n[OK] UPS normal\n[OK] Rack temperatures normal\n[  ] Main Office route restored\n[  ] Final verification complete\n[  ] Shutdown authorised\n\nCurrent state: KEEP IN SERVICE.\n\nNo server fault explains the Main Office terminal's missing connection.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS14, 17U, "TS-14-RS-0190", "UPS & Rack Status Summary", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nUPS & RACK STATUS SUMMARY\n\nUPS load: normal\nBattery status: serviceable\nRack power: stable\nTemperature: normal\nDrive alarms: none\nNetwork core: active\n\nClosure work has removed non-essential equipment from adjacent spaces, but the server rack remains in normal operating state.\n\nThe anti-static strap and spare caddy remain on the Server Room shelving until technical release.\n\nNo abnormal power event is recorded before the suppression discharge.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS18, 2U, "TS-18-RS-0035", "Server Room Cable Riser Maintenance Log", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T048, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nSERVER ROOM CABLE RISER MAINTENANCE LOG\n\nFriday work: restore archive-terminal circuit N-17.\n\n14:05  Route confirmed at riser.\n14:10  Cable tester connected.\n14:14  Damaged/compressed section identified.\n14:18  Network cable partly freed from shared bundle.\n14:22  Adjacent control wiring observed in same route.\n14:24  Work paused briefly to check labels.\n14:27  Cable bundle repositioned for access.\n14:29  Site alarm / suppression discharge. Work abandoned.\n\nFacilities isolation signature was not present on the work sheet at the time of evacuation.\n\nTools and cable were left as found after the alarm.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS18, 5U, "TS-18-RS-0067", "Suppression Event Diagnostic", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T049, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nSUPPRESSION EVENT DIAGNOSTIC\n\nControl diagnostic recovered after the Server Room discharge.\n\nFire detection state before release: NORMAL\nHeat detection state before release: NORMAL\nManual release input: ACTIVE at 14:28:49\nRelease logic response: VALID\nVentilation interlock: OPERATED\nHalon discharge: CONFIRMED\n\nThe diagnostic identifies the manual-release electrical channel as the initiating input.\n\nIt does not show a manual switch being deliberately operated.\n\nFurther examination required:\ntrace the manual-input circuit through the cable-riser work area.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS18, 8U, "TS-18-RS-0082", "Post-Discharge System Recovery Summary", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T050, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nPOST-DISCHARGE SYSTEM RECOVERY SUMMARY\n\nServer services survived the suppression event and controlled re-entry.\n\nInitial recovery:\n- verify atmosphere safe;\n- inspect rack power and UPS;\n- preserve suppression diagnostic;\n- leave cable-riser work undisturbed;\n- confirm backups intact;\n- prevent automatic overwrite of relevant logs.\n\nNo evidence of fire damage or server failure was found.\n\nTechnical investigation priority:\ncompare the manual-release wiring path with the exact network cable area being worked immediately before discharge.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS18, 10U, "TS-18-RS-0109", "Cable Remediation Work Sheet", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nCABLE REMEDIATION WORK SHEET\n\nCircuit N-17 showed movement-sensitive failure at the Server Room riser.\n\nPhysical condition after incident:\n- network cable partly withdrawn;\n- outer jacket compressed at bundle crossing;\n- adjacent legacy control pair displaced from its previous lay;\n- temporary tools still present;\n- no deliberate cut observed.\n\nThe network cable and suppression-control pair occupy the same constrained working space.\n\nBefore further repair:\nphotograph, label and test both circuits independently.\n\nDo not restore neat cable dressing until the incident condition has been recorded.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS18, 13U, "TS-18-RS-0146", "Manual Release Input Trace", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nMANUAL RELEASE INPUT TRACE\n\nThe suppression manual-release input was traced from the control logic through the Server Room cable riser.\n\nContinuity testing identified an intermittent condition in the section adjacent to network circuit N-17.\n\nWhen the affected bundle is moved, the manual-input circuit can momentarily present the same electrical state as an intentional release command.\n\nThe behaviour reproduces the type of input recorded at 14:28:49.\n\nTest performed under safe isolation with discharge output disabled.\n\nFinding requires comparison with the pre-incident Facilities service note, which records earlier instability under cable movement.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS18, 16U, "TS-18-RS-0183", "Server Room Recovery Checklist", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nSERVER ROOM RECOVERY CHECKLIST\n\n[OK] Atmosphere declared safe\n[OK] Server power stable\n[OK] Backup media intact\n[OK] Diagnostic logs preserved\n[OK] Cable-riser condition recorded\n[OK] Manual-release circuit safely isolated\n[OK] Network fault area identified\n[  ] Permanent cable repair\n[  ] Suppression-control repair\n[  ] Final archive verification\n[  ] Closure release\n\nNo permanent repair is to begin until Security accepts the incident documentation.\n\nPreserve first. Repair second.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS18, 18U, "TS-18-RS-0193", "Halon Control Wiring Note", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nHALON CONTROL WIRING NOTE\n\nThe Server Room suppression system uses a manual-release electrical path that shares the service riser with older network cabling.\n\nThe circuits are functionally separate but were installed close together and have been altered at different times.\n\nFacilities records show the manual path remained connected through final closure because the Server Room stayed operational. A Thursday service note also records a brief unstable manual-input indication while adjacent cabling was disturbed.\n\nRecommendation:\nreroute or mechanically separate the control pair during permanent remediation.\n\n\"Separate systems\" is an electrical description, not always a physical one.", false, false },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_TS18, 21U, "TS-18-RS-0230", "Final Technical Reconstruction", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT OF RECORDS\nTECHNOLOGY SERVICES\nFINAL TECHNICAL RECONSTRUCTION\n\nSubject: Server Room Halon discharge, final Friday.\n\nEstablished sequence:\n\n1. The Main Office archive terminal had a genuine fixed-route network fault.\n2. The fault was localised to circuit N-17 at the Server Room cable riser.\n3. The riser also carried the still-connected suppression manual-release circuit.\n4. Facilities had previously recorded manual-input instability when adjacent cabling was moved.\n5. Network remediation disturbed the shared bundle immediately before the incident.\n6. Suppression diagnostics recorded no preceding fire condition and identified the manual-release electrical channel.\n7. Isolated testing reproduced a release-state input when the affected wiring was disturbed.\n\nTechnical conclusion:\nThe discharge was initiated accidentally when cable-remediation work disturbed the still-connected manual-release circuit. No deliberate operation of the suppression control is required to explain the event.\n\nThis conclusion addresses mechanism. Questions of procedure, isolation and responsibility remain matters for the closure review.", false, false },
